  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Achieve Onchocerciasis Elimination in the Americas (Achieve OEA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Global Health (GH)):  Funds will support the complete elimination of onchocerciasis (River Blindness) in the Americas. Onchocerciasis only remains in one area of the Americas, signifying a 95% reduction of disease. With 5% burden remaining, Achieve OEA provides technical and programmatic assistance to implement mass treatment campaigns with the goal of interrupting onchocerciasis transmission and achieving full elimination of this disease in the Americas. USAID has supported the control and elimination of the most common neglected tropical diseases since 2006. $742,582 of FY24 funds will be attriubed to Achieve OEA activities in Central America, Guatemala. ..USAID support through Achieve OEA helps to provide training to indigenous health agents (IHAs), as well as increase their numbers and gender balance. IHAs play a critical role in the program by providing directly, or helping health teams to provide, ivermectin treatments to prevent onchocerciasis. They offer cultural knowledge, translation skills, and serve as guides in the Amazon Rain Forest. Support will also fund an anthropologist to help determine culturally appropriate ways to increase IHA participation, particularly female IHAs who currently make up about 5% of all IHAs. .</narrative>
  </description>
